### Why This Is Asked
This question assesses fundamental Android architecture skills: persistence with Room, data flow through the Repository and ViewModel pattern, and UI binding with RecyclerView. It also verifies understanding of rotation resilience and basic event handling.

### Key Concepts
- Room entities and DAOs for local persistence
- Repository pattern for data abstraction
- ViewModel with LiveData for reactive UI updates
- RecyclerView with Adapter for efficient list rendering
- Basic input handling and state retention across configuration changes

### Code Example
```kotlin
@Entity(tableName = "tasks")
data class TaskEntity(
    @PrimaryKey(autoGenerate = true)
    val id: Long = 0,
    val text: String,
    val done: Boolean = false
)

@Dao
interface TaskDao {
    @Query("SELECT * FROM tasks")
    fun getAllTasks(): LiveData<List<TaskEntity>>

    @Insert
    suspend fun insert(task: TaskEntity)
}

class TaskRepository(private val taskDao: TaskDao) {
    fun getAllTasks(): LiveData<List<TaskEntity>> = taskDao.getAllTasks()

    suspend fun insert(task: TaskEntity) = taskDao.insert(task)
}

class TaskViewModel(private val repository: TaskRepository) : ViewModel() {
    val allTasks: LiveData<List<TaskEntity>> = repository.getAllTasks()

    fun addTask(text: String) {
        if (text.isBlank()) return
        viewModelScope.launch {
            repository.insert(TaskEntity(text = text))
        }
    }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This evaluates the ability to design a compact, realistic offline-first feature using core Android components (Room, WorkManager) and basic security practices, plus a practical testing approach.

## Key Concepts

- Room data model and DAO design
- WorkManager constraints for Wi-Fi-based synchronization
- Android Keystore encryption fundamentals
- Local notification integration and idempotent sync patterns

## Code Example

```kotlin
@Entity(tableName = "articles")
data class Article(
  @PrimaryKey val id: String,
  val title: String,
  val bodyEncrypted: ByteArray,
  val timestamp: Long,
  val source: String
)

@Dao
interface ArticleDao {
  @Insert(onConflict = OnConflictStrategy.REPLACE)
  suspend fun upsertArticles(articles: List<Article>)

  @Query("SELECT * FROM articles ORDER BY timestamp DESC")
  fun getAllArticles(): Flow<List<Article>>
}

class SyncWorker(
  context: Context,
  params: WorkerParameters
) : CoroutineWorker(context, params) {

  override suspend fun doWork(): Result {
    return try {
      val articles = fetchArticles()
      val encryptedArticles = articles.map { encryptArticle(it) }
      articleDao.upsertArticles(encryptedArticles)
      showNotification(articles.size)
      Result.success()
    } catch (e: Exception) {
      Result.retry()
    }
  }
}

val workConstraints = Constraints.Builder()
  .setRequiredNetworkType(NetworkType.UNMETERED)
  .setRequiresBatteryNotLow(true)
  .build()

PeriodicWorkRequestBuilder<SyncWorker>(1, TimeUnit.HOURS)
  .setConstraints(workConstraints)
  .build()
```

